Java 8 is one of the most important versions for interviews. The easiest way to remember its features is:

🚀 Major Java 8 Features
1. Lambda Expression ⭐⭐⭐

Allows you to write functions in a shorter way.

Before Java 8:

List<String> names = Arrays.asList("A", "B", "C");

for (String name : names) {
    System.out.println(name);
}

Java 8:

names.forEach(name -> System.out.println(name));

Trick: Lambda = ->

2. Functional Interface ⭐⭐⭐

An interface having exactly one abstract method.

@FunctionalInterface
interface Calculator {
    int add(int a, int b);
}

Using lambda:

Calculator c = (a, b) -> a + b;

System.out.println(c.add(10, 20));

Common built-in functional interfaces:

Predicate<T>  → boolean
Function<T,R> → R
Consumer<T>   → void
Supplier<T>   → T

Easy trick:

Predicate = test
Function = convert
Consumer = consume
Supplier = supply

3. Stream API ⭐⭐⭐

Used for processing collections.

List<Integer> list = Arrays.asList(1, 2, 3, 4, 5);

list.stream()
    .filter(x -> x % 2 == 0)
    .forEach(System.out::println);

Output:

2
4

Important Stream methods:

filter()
map()
flatMap()
sorted()
distinct()
limit()
skip()
reduce()
collect()
forEach()
count()
4. Method Reference ⭐⭐

Shorter form of lambda.

Instead of:

names.forEach(x -> System.out.println(x));

Use:

names.forEach(System.out::println);

Syntax:

ClassName::methodName
5. Optional ⭐⭐⭐

Helps reduce NullPointerException.

Optional<String> name = Optional.ofNullable(null);

name.ifPresent(System.out::println);

Other methods:

isPresent()
orElse()
orElseGet()
orElseThrow()
ifPresent()
map()
filter()
6. Default Methods in Interface ⭐⭐⭐

Before Java 8, interfaces couldn't have method implementations.

Java 8:

interface Vehicle {

    default void start() {
        System.out.println("Vehicle started");
    }
}

A class can use it without implementing the method.

7. Static Methods in Interface

Java 8 allows static methods inside interfaces.

interface Test {

    static void display() {
        System.out.println("Hello");
    }
}

Call:

Test.display();
8. Date and Time API ⭐⭐⭐

Java 8 introduced the modern java.time API.

Instead of older:

Date
Calendar

Use:

LocalDate
LocalTime
LocalDateTime
ZonedDateTime
Instant
Period
Duration

Example:

LocalDate date = LocalDate.now();

System.out.println(date);
9. CompletableFuture ⭐⭐⭐

Used for asynchronous programming.

CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {
    return "Hello";
});

Useful for:

Async operations
Parallel tasks
Non-blocking workflows
Combining async operations
10. Nashorn JavaScript Engine

Java 8 introduced the Nashorn JavaScript engine for executing JavaScript inside the JVM.

Note: Nashorn was later deprecated and removed from the JDK.

🔥 Java 8 Interview Cheat Sheet

Remember:

Java 8
  ↓
Lambda
  ↓
Functional Interface
  ↓
Stream API
  ↓
Method Reference
  ↓
Optional
  ↓
Default + Static Interface Methods
  ↓
New Date/Time API
  ↓
CompletableFuture
Most important for your Java interviews

Given your Java + Spring Boot interview preparation, prioritize these:

1. Lambda → 2. Functional Interface → 3. Stream → 4. Optional → 5. Method Reference → 6. Default Methods → 7. CompletableFuture

And for Streams, make sure you can explain:

filter()
map()
flatMap()
sorted()
distinct()
limit()
skip()
reduce()
collect()

especially intermediate vs terminal operations.